      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Changing X among Si, Mn, and Al controls interfacial stress development at the oxide/metal junction.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Si-containing CrFeCoNiX preferentially forms SiO2.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10384371::web::028::4_3_oxidation_in_air"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The SiO2 scale is slow-growing and dense and suppresses rapid diffusion.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Al-containing alloys form protective Al2O3 scales that grow slowly and resist high-temperature oxidation and corrosion.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11169556::web::003::introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "SiO2 and Al2O3 minimize strain mismatch and stress buildup at the oxide/metal interface.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mn has high mobility and undergoes rapid outward cation diffusion during oxidation of CrFeCoNiMn.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11169556::web::002::introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mn promotes Mn-rich layered or mixed oxides and accelerates oxide growth.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11169556::web::002::introduction",
        "PMC10384371::web::028::4_3_oxidation_in_air"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mn-rich mixed oxides are less dense than the Si- or Al-rich protective scales.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Rapid formation of Mn-rich oxides produces elevated interfacial stresses that drive cracking and spallation.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The relevant structural mediators are oxide growth kinetics, oxide density, and the oxide/metal interfacial stress state.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11169556::web::002::introduction",
        "PMC11169556::web::003::introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Under identical exposure conditions, Si- and Al-containing alloys will form stable, coherent, adherent scales, whereas Mn-containing alloys will be more susceptible to cracking and spallation.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11169556::web::002::introduction",
        "PMC11169556::web::003::introduction",
        "PMC10384371::web::028::4_3_oxidation_in_air"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Si, Mn, and Al variants are to be compared while all other compositional parameters are held constant.",
